= Authentication =

== Overview ==
'''Authentication''' is the process of establishing confidence that a claimant controls or corresponds to an asserted identity, account, credential, or authenticator under a defined system.

Authentication answers a question such as “is this claimant the enrolled subscriber or account holder?” Systems can authenticate people, devices, software, or services using passwords, cryptographic keys, tokens, biometrics, or combinations of evidence.

Authentication does not decide what an authenticated subject is allowed to do. That is the role of authorization.

== Boundaries ==
* authentication ≠ authorization
* authentication ≠ identity proofing
* authentication ≠ proof of real-world identity in every system

